.TH DIGINET-CENSUS 1 2026-11-13 "libdiginet" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diginet-census \- every control of a Digidesign Control|24 or ProControl, checked one by one
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diginet-census
.B \-i
.I interface
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B diginet-census
.B \-\-fd
.I n
.B \-\-mac
.I mac
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B diginet-census
.B \-\-any
.RB [ \-\-helper
.IR path ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diginet-census
wakes the desk cabled to
.I interface
and walks the library's inventory of its controls in order, strip by strip, then the jog wheel and
the counter, then the section buttons zone by zone. For a control the desk sends (a fader, a touch
cap, a button, a V-Pot, the jog) it tells the operator what to do and waits for the desk; what comes
is decoded and compared with the inventory. For a control the host writes (a fader motor, a lamp, a
ring, a meter, the automation LEDs, a scribble strip, the counter) it writes the frame that exercises
it, asks whether the desk shows it, and clears it.
.PP
The operator answers on standard input: Enter or
.B y
for seen,
.B n
for nothing happened or nothing shows,
.B s
to skip the control,
.B q
to stop the census where it is.
.PP
Three files are written to the output directory:
.BR census.md ,
the report with one row per control and the tally;
.BR census-bodies.txt ,
one line per control the desk sent, its name and the bytes, in the golden format the test suite
reads back; and
.BR census-frames.txt ,
every desk frame raw.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-i " interface"
The interface the desk is cabled to; needs cap_net_raw.
.TP
.BI \-\-fd " n " \-\-mac " mac"
A descriptor that already carries the desk's frames, and the host MAC to use.
.TP
.B \-\-any
One packet socket for every interface; the desk on whichever interface it appears.
.TP
.BI \-\-helper " path"
With
.BR \-\-any :
get the socket from this helper instead of opening it.
.TP
.BI \-\-desk " mac"
With
.BR \-\-any :
this desk only.
.TP
.BI \-\-checksum " zero\fR|\fPsum"
The header checksum of our frames (default sum).
.TP
.BI \-\-keepalive " seconds"
The keepalive period (default 2).
.TP
.BI \-\-wait " seconds"
How long to wait for the desk's announce (default 15).
.TP
.BI \-\-answer " seconds"
How long to wait for the desk or the operator at each control (default 60).
.TP
.BI \-\-settle " ms"
The pause after an input control, for its release and the rest of its motion (default 300).
.TP
.BI \-\-only " in\fR|\fPout\fR|\fPstrips\fR|\fPsections"
Walk that part of the inventory only.
.TP
.BI \-\-strips " n"
Walk the first
.I n
strips only.
.TP
.BI \-\-from " name"
Start at the control with this name (as in the report).
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-out " dir"
Where the three files go (default the current directory).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when every control walked passed or was skipped; 1 when one was a mismatch, missing or failed;
2 bad usage or no socket; 3 the desk is in another host's session; 4 no desk announced; 5 the desk
did not ACK a write.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diginet-probe (1),
.BR diginet-packet-helper (1).
The census and how its record becomes a test: docs/census.md in the libdiginet sources.
